  <!-- ========== INSIDE IRAN ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · ~200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>Iranian state media devoted nearly all broadcast time between 4–7&#160;July to the state funeral for Ali Khamenei, with live coverage of processions in Tehran, Qom, and Mashhad. IRNA and Tasnim published official memorial posters featuring Mojtaba Khamenei alongside quotations attributed to his father, but neither outlet carried a live address, verified audio, or directly attributed statement from Mojtaba during the period under review. Press TV international broadcasts framed the funeral turnout as evidence of domestic cohesion and continuity of the Islamic Republic. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
      <p>Kayhan's editorial line during the funeral period characterized the Islamabad Memorandum as a diplomatic achievement by the Islamic Republic rather than a concession. IRGC Commander Major General Hossein Salami gave a televised address on 5&#160;July describing the MOU as recognition of "Iran's strategic depth" and "the failure of maximum pressure." No Iranian state outlet named a specific concession the MOU required from Tehran; the Hormuz transit-toll dispute was absent from domestic state-media coverage throughout the reviewed period. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
      <p>Foreign Ministry Spokesman Esmaeil Baghaei held no press conference after 3&#160;July; his last confirmed briefing addressed the moratorium on diplomatic public statements during the funeral period. Deputy FM Abbas Araghchi's last attributed IRNA statement (2–3&#160;July) called on all parties to adhere to the MOU. Iran's Supreme National Security Council published no communiqu&#233; during the 4–7&#160;July period. No official Iranian communication attributed formal chairmanship of the SNSC to Mojtaba Khamenei since his 9&#160;March installation. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

